/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_DistLayout
 *
 * Each preset exports to its own directory under dist.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildDistFlat Flat Distribution Layout
 *
 * Recommended layout:
 *
 * @code
 * dist/
 * ├── windows_msvc_x64_debug/
 * ├── windows_msvc_x64_release/
 * ├── windows_msvc_x64_coverage/
 * ├── psoc5lp_armgcc_cortex_m3_soft_debug/
 * └── psoc5lp_armgcc_cortex_m3_soft_release/
 * @endcode
 *
 * The preset name should match the dist folder name.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildDistWhy Why dist is segmented
 *
 * Precompiled libraries are not universal.
 *
 * Compatibility depends on:
 *
 * - operating system,
 * - compiler/toolchain,
 * - architecture,
 * - ABI,
 * - build configuration,
 * - feature macros.
 *
 * Therefore, each build configuration must have a separate distribution folder.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildDistInstalledContent Typical Installed Content
 *
 * A Foundation distribution may contain:
 *
 * @code
 * dist/<preset>/
 * ├── include/
 * ├── lib/
 * └── cmake/
 * @endcode
 *
 * The include directory contains installed headers.
 * The lib directory contains the static library.
 * The cmake directory may contain package configuration files.
 */
